        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1840060
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-16T03:50:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Cound you explain more about the security hole?",
      "parentUuid": "e28814ba_b6b19bec",
      "revId": "5e5cc843b68dd84217ac1d54fde69780b87404fb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "23d74d61_2acd83db",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1176763
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-17T17:59:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I meant, if we allow to add any hook in filesystem, custom vendor module is easily able to retrieve or modify the user contents of the file which hasn\u0027t been encrypted at all. Basically, as a f2fs maintainer, I\u0027ve concerned that the hook with any unknown hacks will eventually affect the f2fs reputation in the world. Hence, please consider upstream patches aligned to your project schedule in advance. All the other vendors have been doing like that, as we have no vendor hook currently.",
      "parentUuid": "1f2a6a9f_e4a250a5",
      "revId": "5e5cc843b68dd84217ac1d54fde69780b87404fb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
